--TEST--
Inside a method, a `propertyPath<static>` parameter is the path's text, so the body converts it with `as propertyPath<self>` before `Core\Reflect::steps` reads it — `rule:statements/static-is-a-member-modifier`, `rule:core-classes/str-parts-and-reflect-steps`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Inside the method, `$path` is a `string`.
// `as propertyPath<self>` checks it against `Model` while the program runs.
class Model {
    public int $id = 0;

    public static function describe(propertyPath<static> $path): void {
        var $checked = $path as propertyPath<self>;
        foreach (Core\Reflect::steps($checked) as var $step) {
            echo $step->name(), ": ", $step->type() ?? "no type", "\n";
        }
    }
}

class Category extends Model {
    public ?Category $parent = null;
}

Category::describe("id");
// `parent` is declared on `Category` and not on `Model`, so the conversion fails.
try {
    Category::describe("parent.id");
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo "not a path of Model\n";
}
--EXPECT--
id: int
not a path of Model
